Description: GtkGLArea: stereo, one view per eye on a subsurface declared as stereo content
 GtkGLArea gains a stereo property. A stereo area emits its render signal
 twice for each frame, the left view first, each time into a framebuffer of
 the area's size, and gtk_gl_area_get_current_eye() tells which view the
 handler draws. The two views are copied side by side into one texture, twice
 the width of the area and opaque, which goes to the compositor on a
 subsurface of its own (the path GtkGraphicsOffload takes), declared as full
 side by side stereo content with kde_stereo_content_v1 (version 2 or later:
 the surface is one view wide, so the area keeps its size). The rest of the
 window stays the window's own surface, drawn once.
 .
 An area that asks for stereo and cannot show it per eye says so: it logs the
 reason once, sets stereo-error, keeps stereo-shown FALSE and renders the left
 view alone as an area without stereo does. GSK's offload takes the whole
 texture for a stereo subsurface, and where GTK cannot offload it the clip the
 area draws it with leaves the left view alone, so the two views are never
 shown side by side in the area's place.
 .
 An area that does not ask for stereo behaves as before: nothing is created,
 declared or bound for it.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-07
